    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The full suite ran green and the new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` acceptance test passes.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe soft \"possible duplicate\" flag on owner creation, following the codebase's established pattern for creation-time observations (namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning): compute against existing owners in a pipeline `Assign` step, persist on the entity, and expose via the MapStruct mapper.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two readOnly fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These generate onto `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted field `Integer possibleDuplicateOf` (`@Column possible_duplicate_of`) with getter/setter. I persist only the id and derive the boolean, since `possibleDuplicate` is exactly \"an id is present\" \u2014 no redundant column.\n\n3. **DB schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql), needed because the test GETs the owner back by id.\n\n4. **`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 single-responsibility step mirroring `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`: scans pre-existing owners for one sharing the built owner's last name (case-insensitive, per house style) and postcode but with a *different* telephone, and records the lowest matching id for determinism. Guards against a null postcode (can't share a postcode). Runs before `save`, so it never self-matches.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignPossibleDuplicate` between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `toOwnerDto` maps `possibleDuplicateOf` directly and derives `possibleDuplicate` via a small `possibleDuplicate(owner)` default method (`possibleDuplicateOf != null`, always a real true/false); `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores the new field since it's pipeline-assigned, not part of the request.\n\nThe existing hard-duplicate rule (`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`, keyed on telephone|email|householdId) already lets a same-lastName/postcode/different-telephone owner through \u2014 so this change only adds the flagging, leaving that behavior and every other rule untouched.",
